      "content": "Choose the one correct answer for each item.\n\n1. Two mutually exclusive events with positive probabilities are ____ dependent.\nA. Always  B. Sometimes  C. Never\n\n2. ____ is a numerical measure of the chance that an uncertain event will occur.\nA. Random experiment  B. Sample space  C. Probability  D. Complement  E. Population\n\n3. Which condition guarantees that $A$ and $B$ are independent?\nA. They are mutually exclusive.  B. $P(A)$ is not influenced by $P(B)$.  C. $P(A\\cap B)=0$.  D. $P(A\\mid B)=P(A)$.  E. Both B and D.\n\n4. For independent events, ____ their probabilities to obtain the intersection probability.\nA. Divide  B. Add  C. Multiply  D. Subtract\n\n5. Events that cannot occur simultaneously are called _____.\nA. Independent  B. Mutually exclusive  C. Intersections  D. Unions\n\n6. If $A$ and $B$ are independent, which expression equals $P(A\\cap B)$?\nA. $P(A)P(B)$  B. $P(A)P(B\\mid A)$  C. $P(B)P(A\\mid B)$  D. All of the above",
